[{"location":"#RandomFunctions","page":"Home","title":"RandomFunctions","text":"Documentation for RandomFunctions.\n\n","category":"section"},{"location":"#RandomFunctions.ComposedSampler","page":"Home","title":"RandomFunctions.ComposedSampler","text":"ComposedSampler <: FunctionSampler\nComposedSampler(::InputSampler, ::OutputSampler)\n\nA FunctionSampler composed of an InputSampler and an OutputSampler.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"#RandomFunctions.FunctionData","page":"Home","title":"RandomFunctions.FunctionData","text":"FunctionData(context_x, context_y, target_x, target_y)\n\nA struct to hold the context and target data of sampled functions.\n\nFields\n\ncontext_x::AbstractArray{<:Real, 3}: shape (xdim, ncontextpoints, nbatch)\ncontext_y::AbstractArray{<:Real, 3}: shape (ydim, ncontextpoints, nbatch)\ntarget_x::AbstractArray{<:Real, 3}: shape (xdim, ntargetpoints, nbatch)\ntarget_y::AbstractArray{<:Real, 3}: shape (ydim, ntargetpoints, nbatch)\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"#RandomFunctions.FunctionSampler","page":"Home","title":"RandomFunctions.FunctionSampler","text":"FunctionSampler\n\nAn abstract type for sampling functions.\n\nEach subtype of FunctionSampler should implement the following methods:\n\nsample(::FunctionSampler, n_context::Int, n_target::Int, n_batch::Int) -> ::FunctionData\nx_dim(::FunctionSampler) -> Int\ny_dim(::FunctionSampler) -> Int\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"#RandomFunctions.GPSampler","page":"Home","title":"RandomFunctions.GPSampler","text":"GPSampler(; kwargs...)\n\nA sampler for generating 1D Gaussian Process (GP) function outputs.\n\nKeywords\n\nkernel::Kernel: The base kernel function for the GP (default: GaussianKernel())\nlength_scale_prior::UnivariateDistribution: Prior distribution for sampling length scales  (default: Uniform(0.1, 1.0)). One length scale is sampled per input dimension.\namplitude_prior::UnivariateDistribution: Prior distribution for sampling the signal amplitude  (default: Uniform(0.1, 1.0))\nnoise_std_prior::UnivariateDistribution: Prior distribution for sampling the noise standard  deviation (default: Dirac(1e-6)). Used for numerical stability.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"#RandomFunctions.InputSampler","page":"Home","title":"RandomFunctions.InputSampler","text":"InputSampler\n\nAn abstract type for sampling input points for functions.\n\nEach subtype of InputSampler should implement the following method:\n\nsample(::InputSampler, n_context::Int, n_target::Int, n_batch::Int) -> (x_context, x_target)\nx_dim(::InputSampler) -> Int\n\nSee also FunctionData for the expected shapes of the input and output arrays.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"#RandomFunctions.OutputSampler","page":"Home","title":"RandomFunctions.OutputSampler","text":"OutputSampler\n\nAn abstract type for sampling output values for functions.\n\nEach subtype of OutputSampler should implement the following method:\n\nsample(::OutputSampler, x_context, x_target) -> (y_context, y_target)\ny_dim(::OutputSampler) -> Int\n\nSee also FunctionData for the expected shapes of the input and output arrays.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"#RandomFunctions.sample","page":"Home","title":"RandomFunctions.sample","text":"sample(sampler::FunctionSampler, n_context::Int, n_target::Int, n_batch::Int) -> FunctionData\nsample(sampler::InputSampler, n_context::Int, n_target::Int, n_batch::Int) -> (x_context, x_target)\nsample(sampler::OutputSampler, x_context, x_target) -> (y_context, y_target)\n\nThe sample function is the main interface for sampling functions, input points, and output values.\n\nSee also FunctionData.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#RandomFunctions.x_dim","page":"Home","title":"RandomFunctions.x_dim","text":"x_dim(::FunctionSampler) -> Int\nx_dim(::InputSampler) -> Int\n\nReturns the dimensionality of the input space for a given sampler.\n\nSee also y_dim.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#RandomFunctions.y_dim","page":"Home","title":"RandomFunctions.y_dim","text":"y_dim(::FunctionSampler) -> Int\ny_dim(::OutputSampler) -> Int\n\nReturns the dimensionality of the output space for a given sampler.\n\nSee also x_dim.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"}]
